  - id: the_levitical_priesthood
    displayName: The Levitical Priesthood
    flavorText: Every high priest is taken from among men and called of God as Aaron
      was, yet the Levitical priests die one after another and must keep offering
      the same sacrifices that can never take away sins.
    tierType: 1
    purpose: Argues that the Levitical/Aaronic priestly system, however divinely
      instituted, could not itself bring perfection or a clear conscience, since
      its priests died and had to be replaced, it required repeated sacrifices, and
      the law under it required a change once the priesthood changed, so it always
      pointed beyond itself to a permanent priest after the order of Melchisedec.
    deliveredByManagerId: 
    managerId: levitical_priesthood_hebrews
    icon: {fileID: 0}
    managerIcon: {fileID: 0}
    baseCost: 976.858520142912
